    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d42">

                <pb facs="0113" n="37" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg37"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 711.9321/1</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Chargé MacMurray to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-07-11">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 11, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>May the notification of abrogation directed by Department’s instruction of May 29
                    be explicitly confined to the second sentence of Article 18 of the Treaty of
                    1858, which alone concerns arrest of seamen?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
